<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jalal al-Din Mangburni</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1231">1231</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Jalal al-Din Khwarazmshah, Jalal al-Din Mingburnu, Jalal ad-Din Manguberdi, Jalal ad-Din Mingburnu, Jalal al-Din Manguberdi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jalal al-Din Mingburnu was the last ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazmian-empire">Khwarazmian Empire</a>. After his father's defeat by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a> he fought on, winning at Parwan in 1221 before being routed on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a>. He then built a new realm in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>, sacking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tbilisi">Tbilisi</a> in 1226, but was defeated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> of Rum and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubids</a> in 1230 and killed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurdistan">Kurdistan</a> in 1231.</p></div>
